{
  "id": "u05-l08",
  "unit": "u05-numbers-time",
  "title": "Days of the week",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "Every day ends in **-বার** (*-bar*) 'day of the week', and the names come from the sun, moon and planets, as in English:\n\n**রবিবার** Sun · **সোমবার** Mon · **মঙ্গলবার** Tue · **বুধবার** Wed · **বৃহস্পতিবার** Thu · **শুক্রবার** Fri · **শনিবার** Sat\n\n**আজ** (*aj*) is 'today'. **আজ কী বার?** = 'What day is it today?' Answer with no verb: **আজ শুক্রবার।**\n\n*Culture:* the weekly holiday is **শুক্রবার**, the day of Jumma prayers. Many offices close on **শনিবার** too, so the working week runs Sunday to Thursday.",
  "vocab": [
